 de l'industrie 3.jpg","author":"DiscoA340","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Back_of_the_Cit%C3%A9_des_sciences_et_de_l%27industrie_3.jpg","sourceSha1":"c819d5097c6d86116e84e5a92d0f1ceb391fdbab","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Exterior; industrial hall and roof trusses"},{"title":"File:Back of the Cité des sciences et de l'industrie 4.jpg","author":"DiscoA340","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Back_of_the_Cit%C3%A9_des_sciences_et_de_l%27industrie_4.jpg","sourceSha1":"c9ea14400ca65a2331d381a29adbf841b8105ea3","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Exterior; industrial hall and roof trusses"},{"title":"File:Cité des Sciences @ La Villette @ Paris (33549562400).jpg","author":"Guilhem Vellut from Paris, France","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cit%C3%A9_des_Sciences_@_La_Villette_@_Paris_(33549562400).jpg","sourceSha1":"e3ea8e9966906c9eda5a10bae74e1d3aaa82cacf","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Exterior; industrial hall and roof trusses"}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["The complete OSM outline fixes the hall plan, including projecting structural piers. The outline height of 34 m sets the main roof; the four mapped roof structures retain their 38/40 m tops.","The reviewed CC BY 2.0 photograph references/03.jpg establishes a broad industrial hall with exposed roof trusses, tall glazed bays and a regular structural rhythm. References 01/02 confirm the long elevation. Truss section, 5.4 m depth, 16 m panel rhythm and glazing dimensions are map-scale inferences, not survey measurements.","Four longitudinal roof truss lines follow the three-bay width of the plan. The material library roof grey substitutes for painted blue steel; windows and mapped rooflights use the approved light-blue palette.","The two mapped circular roof structures begin at the roof datum rather than becoming enclosed cylinders through the interior. The Geode, reflecting pools, bridges and landscaping lie outside this footprint and are omitted.","No photographic textures or interiors. Fine screen mesh, pipework and mullions are reduced to sparse facade divisions; roof trusses remain open geometry."],"source":{"url":"/objects/f794837e127210acbdf64c91a0472e8b8d601c9e54c738c19844c93b27f68f24/source.blend.gz","bytes":127260,"sha256":"f794837e127210acbdf64c91a0472e8b8d601c9e54c738c19844c93b27f68f24"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/c90e0d16d222954ed2486c2cff76fbed10963ed9c3e8774935b6a66fb1b265b2/spatial-source.json","bytes":10967,"sha256":"c90e0d16d222954ed2486c2cff76fbed10963ed9c3e8774935b6a66fb1b265b2"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/ae2df33a0a9fcd32253232b8a24ee94b6d452a98117c0200d395297ea374df5e/preview.webp","bytes":8422,"sha256":"ae2df33a0a9fcd32253232b8a24ee94b6d452a98117c0200d395297ea374df5e"},"revision":"7fee3f853bfec940ac54203a5c8edaffdf62629f63808d9a3d7ef234c7ea2efc","publicationRevision":"362ea5e31c2a338a5fee81289c7d318d63281aa75f882e370d43f4f0ab7c29dc","bounds":[2.3859872,48.8945229,2.3899516,48.8968486],"approved":false,"materialLibrary":{"schemaVersion":1,"sha256":"121eb8f661cd76df4f6ea710947bfce0cace2e6aef7fda643b2d4407a7fbb3c9","url":"/materials/121eb8f661cd76df4f6ea710947bfce0cace2e6aef7fda643b2d4407a7fbb3c9.json"},"metadata":"/assets/cite-des-sciences/362ea5e31c2a33